{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nutlike-biophilic-sheep","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nResearch ticket melancholy-couped-turkey concluded that the fixed-count compaction cadence (`compact.threshold`, default 10) makes retained full-state snapshot bytes grow **Θ(N²)** for a growing ticket (measured: 5.36 GB of retired-snapshot bytes at 8,000 events). It recommends a **byte/replay-cost-aware cadence** (`compact_plan.needs_folding` folds when `pending_source_bytes >= alpha * active_snapshot_bytes`, plus a count floor and the existing first-snapshot arm), gated by a new default-off `compact.snapshot_alpha` config, which bounds retained-snapshot bytes to **Θ(N)** (~1/alpha amplification; 344× reduction at alpha=1.0) while keeping read cost within (1+alpha)× of a snapshot load. All ADR-0035 contracts (conservative horizon, rebuild-on-stray, crash recovery, mixed-version rollback, two-clone union) are preserved because only the WHEN trigger changes.\n\nThis is a **design decision** and per AC5 of the research ticket must NOT be implemented until an ADR completes RESEARCH → DRAFT → HOLD → MERGE with human approval.\n\n## Plan\n- Author an ADR for the byte/replay-cost-aware snapshot cadence + `compact.snapshot_alpha` config; carry it through RESEARCH → DRAFT → HOLD → MERGE with human sign-off.\n- Add a two-clone reconvergence test proving byte-cost cadence divergence is absorbed by merge-as-union + gap-timestamp + rebuild-on-stray (the one contract the single-clone benchmark could not exercise).\n- Calibrate `alpha` against the live store's ticket-size distribution.\n- Once the ADR MERGEs, decompose implementation into independently reviewable tasks with binary acceptance criteria (config field + coercer; `needs_folding` trigger; default-off rollback safety; tests).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] An ADR for the adaptive snapshot cadence is authored and completes RESEARCH → DRAFT → HOLD → MERGE with recorded human approval: `checked: docs/adr/ contains the merged ADR`.\n- [ ] A two-clone reconvergence test for byte-cost cadence divergence exists and passes.\n- [ ] `alpha` default is calibrated and justified against the live ticket-size distribution.\n- [ ] Implementation is decomposed into linked child tasks, each with binary acceptance criteria, before any code lands.\n\nDO NOT start implementation before the ADR reaches MERGE. Escalated from melancholy-couped-turkey research.","id":"da70-18a5-898d-47ea","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"ADR + implement adaptive byte/replay-cost snapshot cadence (compact.snapshot_alpha)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787569449741740001,"uuid":"e25b4e85-a5ab-4983-8e7c-7224d42cfe48"}